{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table","id":923927,"title":"[Solar-ish] Which castes do you want to see least at your table?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-30T10:22:42-07:00","id":923927,"title":"[Solar-ish] Which castes do you want to see least at your table?","content":"Exalted may not be Dungeons and Dragons, but often times we take some of our assumptions about Caste as though they were &quot;class&quot;. So I decided to follow that line of thinking and came to an interesting question. In D+D, as a player, sometimes when another player comes into the game with particular classes you wince a little. Maybe because you think the class is broken? too weak and will &quot;drag down the group&quot;? That people who disrupt games tend to play that class a lot? Things like that. So lets port this idea over to Exalted.<br /> <br /> Which, if any of the Solar Castes, set off red flags or warning bells as a fellow player in a group?<br /> How about as an ST?<br /> What about other Caste-level choices in Exalted for other splats (using prior edition knowledge)?<br /> <br /> Some pre-rebuttal ahead of time:<br /> <br /> Yes, I know there are only 5 castes. Yes, I know that problematic behavior is not inherently isolated to Caste choices. This is a question of experiences and preferences. Yes, I know there is an aesthetic thing with the &quot;perfect circle&quot; so there is social pressure not to demonize any one caste. Even so, natural reactions to experiences interest me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T10:27:08-07:00","id":923930,"title":"","content":"Not really. The castes are FAR too broad with FAR too many varieties for one particular Caste to be worth going &quot;Oh this is gonna be a <i>thing</i>-&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, I <i>would</i> get leery of certain concepts in certain games. Like for instance, if it's not a combat-focused game but someone brings in a Dawn with 90% Melee Charms of their initial set to splatter any threat the ST could throw at them. But hell, even something like that could fit if roleplayed well, and if you discuss what's going on and what suits the game then you're probably in the clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T10:28:18-07:00","id":923933,"title":"","content":"Not sure, its kind of hard...Dawn appears often for obvious reasons but at the same time, I wouldn't want Dawn to not feel like the warrior caste anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T10:33:01-07:00","id":923940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=923930#post923930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. The castes are FAR too broad with FAR too many varieties for one particular Caste to be worth going &quot;Oh this is gonna be a <i>thing</i>-&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If I hadn't come to this experience myself, I would say this is probably the answer. However, that being said, across maybe 20 Exalted games, various one-offs, and over a hundred unique players, the Twilight has invariably been the &quot;problem player&quot; about 3/4ths of the time. While I recognize this might not be a problem inherent to the Caste itself; I am interested in exploring commonalities and different experiences which lead to biases.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T10:33:46-07:00","id":923941,"title":"","content":"Well, in WW games in general, I get a bit nervous when someone wants to play something that wasn't on the menu, so to speak. Everybody knows the type. Really, <b>really</b> wants to play a Mage in the Vampire game. Yearns to play an Infernal or an Abyssal in a game the ST set up to be just Solars. That sort of thing usually sets off my problem player radar. Which isn't to say good players never do this. Just that in my experience most of the time it signals a desire to play <i>their</i> game, rather than play with their fellow players and ST.<br /> <br /> I also tend to worry when Castes might justify the proclivities of a given player. There's always that one person who makes the Night Caste so they can't be found by the party and go be The Loner or whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:05:01-07:00","id":923969,"title":"","content":"In previous editions, I found Dawns and Full Moons were often associated with the &quot;ineffective munchkin&quot;, a particular type of problem player who was new to Exalted and thought the fact he could accumulate huge dice pools at chargen was an exploit, not realizing that in rocket-tag combat he was actually just going to get wrecked in the first fight.<br /> <br /> Zeniths tended to signal the uncompromising pain-in-everyone-elses-ass &quot;paladin&quot; type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:18:57-07:00","id":923977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=923941#post923941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in WW games in general, I get a bit nervous when someone wants to play something that wasn't on the menu, so to speak. Everybody knows the type. Really, <b>really</b> wants to play a Mage in the Vampire game. Yearns to play an Infernal or an Abyssal in a game the ST set up to be just Solars. That sort of thing usually sets off my problem player radar. Which isn't to say good players never do this. Just that in my experience most of the time it signals a desire to play <i>their</i> game, rather than play with their fellow players and ST.<br /> <br /> I also tend to worry when Castes might justify the proclivities of a given player. There's always that one person who makes the Night Caste so they can't be found by the party and go be The Loner or whatnot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhg. Been there before exactly as you said it. Had a player join an ongoing Solar game who was practically desperate to be an Abyssal. And not even a redemptive Abyssal. Wanted to work with a death lord and everything. When I informed him the Abyssal was right out and it was a Solar or something not as powerful he grudgingly went with a Solar. The Solar castes have been broad enough to not cause me any trouble. However he wanted to basically make a carbon copy of our Night caste. Annoyingly he didn't even know what our Night's skills and abilities were. Finally convinced him to make a Dawn ninja which we really needed. He still tried to do make it a loner game about his character. Eventually that character became, guess what, an Abyssal in the service of the Mask of Winters. That's the most egregious example but I've had others. I'll bet we all have.<br /> <br /> In another game where I was a player, another player made a social focused character. No big deal. I like for my groups to have someone who covers the basics; fighting, infiltrating, social, and knowledge. However with a less experienced ST the game was 90% him. Annoyingly he went way out of his way to socialize NPCs. For example, the group needed to get a slice of pie from a particular pie maker. Not even a whole pie. One slice. This player socialed every NPC in the establishment until he could convince and acquire every single piece of pie. Partially eaten or not. The game dragged to a crawl. Seriously, his social scenes took longer than combat to resolve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:42:33-07:00","id":923989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=923940#post923940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Twilight has invariably been the &quot;problem player&quot; about 3/4ths of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well since a lot of us are sharing, got any really good stories on Problem Twilights?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:54:23-07:00","id":923999,"title":"","content":"Pretty much an observer here but yeah, I have a related question about the Perfect Circle ideal: Whether in practice it tends to be easier to ST and play a Perfect Circle set up that's the idealised set up for Exalted - same splat methodology, about 5 different areas of role focus within that. Or a set up where you have like, a Slayer, a Dawn, a Dusk, a Full Moon meet up... where you have characters with the same general goal and focus - they're *all* about about the path of the warrior - with slightly different Exalt type variations. If anyone wants to bite on their experiences?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:38:58-07:00","id":924025,"title":"","content":"As an ST: Dawn, and any Supernal combat equivalent to come. I don't mind them as PC adversaries just not as PC's. It just makes balancing combat to weird for my liking.<br /> <br /> In previous games: Any Sidereal in mixed company (please make them more mixed party friendly this time around). // Mind you that's based on a single player but it was a PITA.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/977-major","name":"Major","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar977_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:50:18-07:00","id":924033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=923989#post923989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well since a lot of us are sharing, got any really good stories on Problem Twilights?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I didn't want to overfill the well early on with my own stories before people had a chance to respond and a tone-set had occurred. This might take a second to explain, but I swear it makes sense.<br /> <br /> So, a long time ago, a WW book, I forget which, once was going over &quot;problem player types&quot; and one of them was &quot;The Wallflower&quot;. This is fairly standard stuff.. until they mention a caveat (to paraphrase):<b> &quot;...now if the PLAYER is portraying the CHARACTER as a wallflower, that is incredibly cool...&quot;</b> implying division between whether something is a problem <i>depending on which angle you take it,</i> with the understanding that it fits into the game theme, it's probably fine. It was a good lesson for me at the time and I took it with me moving forward.<br /> <br /> So how does this link to Twilight players and problematic behaviors? You're probably thinking &quot;Twilight players are all wallflowers&quot;. Actually, no, it's the opposite! In my experience, the bad Twilight players I encountered had the problem of conflating in-character elements into their out-of-character behavior, while in-character their characters are fairly boring and drab and scene-stealing at the same time (large scale projects! Crafting scenes! Doing stuff to change the world because I'm SO DAMN SMART&quot;! <br /> <br /> To clarify further, multiple of these Twilight players are, as players, a fount of lore, facts, and general hyper-specific knowledge about Exalted from an OOC perspective, and it's just ASSUMED as a Twilight, they know this stuff, and it is their &quot;role&quot; to act in this hyper-specific and confident manner about this minutae. Almost like the Twilight is the skin they wear to justify their particular brand of annoying gaming, like how Tot above described a Caste managing to play badly to the proclivities of the player. Twilight is the signpost for me that maybe this person might &quot;love the game too much&quot; and have no social sense about scene stealing or making other people's experiences worse with their authority, or wants to use the game to dramatically edit the canon setting with their projects and (importantly), that is the primary or only reason they play.<br /> <br /> I hope this made sense at all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:55:07-07:00","id":924034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Major</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924025#post924025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In previous games: Any Sidereal in mixed company (please make them more mixed party friendly this time around). // Mind you that's based on a single player but it was a PITA.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I always wondered, which is more palatable to the rest of the players/ST:<br /> <br /> A Sidereal PC who actively hides who they are from the other PCs &quot;I'm just your average traveling musician. Nothing to see here.&quot;<br /> A Sidereal PC who doesn't explain anything about what they are but at the same time doesn't hide anything. &quot;It's a long story. I rather not get into it.&quot;<br /> A Sidereal PC that is open about what they are and what a Sidereal is. &quot;I'm the Exalted that Creation forgot about.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 06-30-2016, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:57:39-07:00","id":924037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924034#post924034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always wondered, which is more palatable to the rest of the players/ST:<br /> <br /> A Sidereal PC who actively hides who they are from the other PCs<br /> A Sidereal PC who doesn't explain anything about what they are but at the same time doesn't hide anything<br /> A Sidereal PC that is open about what they are and what a Sidereal is</div> </div> </div> </div>IME, 1 is right out, 2 is only with a good group without trust issues in gaming (hard to find), and 3 is generally fine if we discount all other crossover issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:57:50-07:00","id":924038,"title":"","content":"I don't really run into Castes I don't want to see, if more run into concepts/archtypes I don't want to see. The most common of these being the Murderlight.<br /> <br /> Murderlight: Players who select Twilight for concepts such as &quot;Demon Hunter&quot; or &quot;Exorcist&quot; but only put the barest amount of points/charms into Caste abilities, usually enough for All-Encompassing Sorceror's Sight and the charms that let you fuck up Spirits, and then dump every last point into combat abilities. They claim they're going to play a cerebral character who only uses violence as a last option, but they end up just playing murder-hobos with a forcefield.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, 3E's revamping of the Essence powers DOES cut down on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T13:00:09-07:00","id":924041,"title":"","content":"I find that there are 'bad sterotypes', but nothing that would throw up a red flag to me. It's more like 'if someone is going to play one of these, if they're one of THOSE players, they're probably going to play up on these stereotypes'; so these are just 'if I see someone saying that they have a bad player in this caste, I'm gonna assume it's this issue'<br /> <br /> Dawn: Gotta kill Everything. No Peace, No Negotation. 100% Fatality Rate, kill, maim and murder anything that even slightly stands against you, never give a second chance. Generally gonna be the most 'Murder-hobo', will probably have just 'found' an Artifact somewhere and not really care about it. Most likely to have already killed a Wyld Hunt in their backstory before the game started.<br /> <br /> Zenith: If the Dawn browbeats everyone outside of the group, the Zenith browbeats everyone in it. They play up the fact that only they get messages from the Sun and that this means they expect everyone to fall in line and listen to them immediately; their goals are the most important and they will never change their mind. Most likely to demand the recreation of the First Age. In 2E, expect them to favor Melee and other Combat Stuff and expect the Dawn to allow them to be their equal in combat. Equally likely as the Dawn to forgo redemption in favor of blowing the shit out of everyone.<br /> <br /> Night: Spend as much time as possible hiding from everyone, including the party. The longer the party doesn't even know you exist, the better. Sneak around, try to spend as little time with the party as possible. Lie to the party and otherwise misinform them, be clear that you trust no one and nothing in the party. Often has some other 'boss' they're reporting to. Despite this, will often not actually DO anything; expect them to hide but only hide around the party, instead of going to retrieve information.<br /> <br /> Twilight: Hide in the Manse until you're Essence Five, then churn out infinite Artifacts and built servitors to make everyone else obsolete. Ignore anything that isn't 'know everything about the First Age' and 'Remake the First Age'- tied with Zenith for the whole 'Recreate the First Age'. Most likely to demand trips to Malfeas to make pacts with Demons for artifacts or w/e; I expect plenty of Transhumanism and Industrial Revolution literature and stuff from them.<br /> <br /> Eclipse: Social Fu everyone and everything, the same as the Zenith. Get into fights with the Zenith over who the actual leader of the Circle is, invest in Beaucracy and expect infinite everything to fall into your lap. Use Oaths on Everything you can find, go to Heaven and find Gods to learn whatever charms you can find from Gods, preferably the most overpowered ones. Secretly as munkiny as the Twilight but using the God Charms instead of Crafting stuff<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T13:04:38-07:00","id":924044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924037#post924037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IME, 1 is right out, 2 is only with a good group without trust issues in gaming (hard to find), and 3 is generally fine if we discount all other crossover issues.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I ended up in situation 1 once due to the other Sidereal player wanting to play undercover. My personal preference as Sidereal player is 2 that eventually leads into 3. <br /> <br /> For Arcane Fate, I just hand wave that the non-Sidereal players have been around the Sidereal long enough to remember. As long as the Sidereal is in the room. If they need to describe the Sidereal when the Sidereal is not around, I'd make them do the usual Arcane Fate roll. Or just give the Sidereal a long term Resplendent Destiny at Character Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T13:04:43-07:00","id":924045,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar255_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"255\" data-vbnamecard=\"255\">ParanoiaCombo</a> - Actually, yeah, I get exactly what you're saying. My own personal Twilight doesn't have the fully history of the world memorized, and grew up Immaculate, so I like to THINK I don't fall into that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T13:05:26-07:00","id":924046,"title":"","content":"I haven't so far noticed any Castes that problem players in general are particularly drawn to, only natural inclinations that align a certain Caste with certain <i>types </i>of problem players. Like the annoying &quot;I'm going to be an impish kleptomaniac&quot; is definitely going to be a Night Caste because it mechanically enables the sort of irritating behaviors that the player wants to engage in. And the player who wants to act like an overbearing moralistic bully will be drawn to Zenith. Et cetera. Problem players usually select the character type that they believe best excuses/justifies their bad behavior, or that which will be most likely to shield them from the RL consequences of it.<br /> <br /> But none these are problems with the Caste of the character <i>per se</i>. They're all problems with the player. There are no Castes that I dislike seeing at my table, but there are unquestionably players that I will kick to the curb at warp speed because I have no patience for that nonsense any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T13:07:16-07:00","id":924048,"title":"","content":"I haven't played 3rd edition extensively, but so far Dawn is the caste I am the least excited to see at my table. Having a Dawn with a Supernal combat skill who focuses heavily on combat can create a definite power imbalance at the table, and require you to start having to design encounters around the one super-powerful character who can defeat nearly anything you throw at him, and the rest of the group who's also there, without those other players feeling too much like sidekicks.<br /> <br /> It's not as bad as 2nd edition where you had one Paranoia Combat optimized character and the rest with more or less &quot;realistic&quot; builds (I had that happen once, it was fucking horrible) - 3rd edition is a bit better and even players who aren't &quot;combat kings&quot; can still contribute, but it's still enough of an issue that if someone said they wanted to play a Dawn so they could Supernal (Combat Ability) I would inwardly wince a little bit.<br /> <br /> As to Twilights, the only issue I ever had was a player who was the &quot;Hermit craftsman.&quot; The player wanted everyone to take a couple of years of downtime so he could craft a panoply of 5 dot artifacts for everyone in the group, an airship, essence canons, etc. The player would get annoyed when I would &quot;interrupt&quot; his crafting by forcing his character and the rest of the group to go out on adventures or deal with problems - &quot;We should just wait and deal with everything from a position of absolute power once we have all of our end-game equipment,&quot; was his philosophy, (and to be fair to him he was used to playing games where there wasn't much of a sense of time progression and the party could just sit around and rest for however long they wanted without things really changing) and we ended up clashing a few times because of that.<br /> <br /> But that was more because of the player than his Exalt caste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T13:07:16-07:00","id":924049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924044#post924044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ended up in situation 1 once due to the other Sidereal player wanting to play undercover. My personal preference as Sidereal player is 2 that eventually leads into 3.<br /> <br /> For Arcane Fate, I just hand wave that the non-Sidereal players have been around the Sidereal long enough to remember. As long as the Sidereal is in the room. If they need to describe the Sidereal when the Sidereal is not around, I'd make them do the usual Arcane Fate roll. Or just give the Sidereal a long term Resplendent Destiny at Character Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>We actually had a Sidereal play situation 1 once. It was a hoot. Our other players kept forgetting about him and leaving him behind when they went off to do other stuff, and he kept having to chase us and catch up halfway through the next encounter. He decided fairly quickly to let everyone in on the secret and try to inure them to Arcane Fate as much as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T13:09:24-07:00","id":924052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924034#post924034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Sidereal PC who actively hides who they are from the other PCs &quot;I'm just your average traveling musician. Nothing to see here.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/357759-things-one-is-not-allowed-to-do-in-exalted#post357759\">This feels relevant</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T13:32:37-07:00","id":924061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924045#post924045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar255_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"255\" data-vbnamecard=\"255\">ParanoiaCombo</a> - Actually, yeah, I get exactly what you're saying. My own personal Twilight doesn't have the fully history of the world memorized, and grew up Immaculate, so I like to THINK I don't fall into that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know the character, but I will take your word for it, as you know them best.<br /> <br /> I think the picture I was trying to paint, succinctly, is that Twilight players (ime) tend to act like stereotypical depictions of Twilight behavior in the game, in an OOC manner. Maybe a little bit too much to say about Exalted and not enough just playing, maybe a little bit too much &quot;me&quot; versus &quot;we&quot;. Too much about &quot;figuring out&quot; the game instead of discovering it in-play. Maybe too much covering up their inability to engage with scenarios as presented without meta-knowledge (and then trying to do it anyways). Key words &quot;too much&quot;. I know that can crop up in ANY game in any class, but I feel like Twilights specifically are like this summoning call to a particularly larger set of problem players. Of course, it could just be my sample size, or outlier experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T13:43:30-07:00","id":924070,"title":"","content":"Not really a caste so much as a character type that leans towards one caste (Twilight) but I hate having sorcerers at my table. They constantly want sorcery to be a source of all their... everything. Refuting any limitations, reacting to any consequences from their actions badly, just... bad.<br /> <br /> Literally every player I've played with that wants 'sorcerer' to be a main aspect of their character has been whiny about it, and wanted it to be the easiest path to pure power, wanting to create new initiations that perfectly fit their characters, invent new spells that do exactly what they need, and refusing to accept any limitations. Despite already being incredibly powerful as is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Non-Solar wise: Chosen of Serenity. I fucking hate them. I have ran 4 sidereal games, and played in 7, as well as had a handful of experiences with only a Chosen of Serenity in a mix-splat game. In all but two games (one where I was the Chosen of Serenity!) the Chosen of Serenity has been every bad, childish sex obsessed loose as can be prostitute character that they are stigmatized as. Almost all of them would take 'sexy' ways of fighting, and wear no clothes but oh we have discrete essence armor so we can be basically naked. The worst one I ever played with was an absolutely terrible player who didn't even try to hide that every bit of his (I assume it was a guy, despite playing a girl) character was just a sex joke. Giant E cup breasts, an artifact armor they literally called the 'Victorious Secret' or something like that... ugh.<br /> <br /> I hate Serenities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","user":"KittyEmpress","date":". 06-30-2016, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T13:47:32-07:00","id":924072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924061#post924061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the picture I was trying to paint, succinctly, is that Twilight players (ime) tend to act like stereotypical depictions of Twilight behavior in the game, in an OOC manner. Maybe a little bit too much to say about Exalted and not enough just playing, maybe a little bit too much &quot;me&quot; versus &quot;we&quot;. Too much about &quot;figuring out&quot; the game instead of discovering it in-play. Maybe too much covering up their inability to engage with scenarios as presented without meta-knowledge (and then trying to do it anyways). Key words &quot;too much&quot;. I know that can crop up in ANY game in any class, but I feel like Twilights specifically are like this summoning call to a particularly larger set of problem players. Of course, it could just be my sample size, or outlier experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're saying. I had a very intelligent player who was a rules lawyer, and he knew it. He didn't play a Twilight because he felt it would be too easy for him to fall into the mindset you described.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T13:52:37-07:00","id":924077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924070#post924070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-Solar wise: Chosen of Serenity. I fucking hate them. I have ran 4 sidereal games, and played in 7, as well as had a handful of experiences with only a Chosen of Serenity in a mix-splat game. In all but two games (one where I was the Chosen of Serenity!) the Chosen of Serenity has been every bad, childish sex obsessed loose as can be prostitute character that they are stigmatized as. Almost all of them would take 'sexy' ways of fighting, and wear no clothes but oh we have discrete essence armor so we can be basically naked. The worst one I ever played with was an absolutely terrible player who didn't even try to hide that every bit of his (I assume it was a guy, despite playing a girl) character was just a sex joke. Giant E cup breasts, an artifact armor they literally called the 'Victorious Secret' or something like that... ugh.<br /> <br /> I hate Serenities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. That sucks. Serenity is my favorite Sidereal Caste. Venus' chosen are so much more than prostitutes (not that some of them aren't courtesans). My first Serenity was a Traveling Musician who mourned his dead Solar Son and my second was basically a Righteous Devil cowgirl who carried a set of Flame pieces called &quot;Peacemakers&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T14:07:10-07:00","id":924085,"title":"","content":"The answer that popped immediately to mind was &quot;Night&quot;, because the potential for &quot;OK, I ditch these losers at the gates and stealth my way to the objective&quot; is much too strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T14:10:14-07:00","id":924087,"title":"","content":"This thread reminds me that my group is awesome. In our current game, the Dawn shows restraint and is interesting out of combat, the Twilight is full of curiosity rather than answers, and the Zenith really wants to help people. I've never seen these players come close to a disruptive character, even in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T14:27:39-07:00","id":924096,"title":"","content":"I can safely say Night castes should be giving me warning bells these days. In the last three games I've run, they've been heartless murderers and/or loneliest wolves.<br /> <br /> In the game I wrapped up a year+ ago, only one other PC (who played his Zenith lover) ever knew the Night's real name or face; at least one character was aware he was disguised, but he declined to show her the truth because as it stood there were only three people who knew what he looked like and he could kill them all if he had to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T14:30:08-07:00","id":924098,"title":"","content":"While not actually a problem in either of the two games i'm involved in I see potential problems with trying to balance a supernal-combat dawn with a less-fighty party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T14:55:35-07:00","id":924112,"title":"","content":"I don't actually have any experience with bad players being a problem in Exalted as my players are pretty fabulous. I think someone else said it well when they said that the problem they run into is balancing combat when you've got someone whose Supernal Melee means they have a perfect Parry of 7 versus basically everything. It's not bad, it's not wrong, it's not really out of flavor, but it can be tough to do combat and have it feel as exciting when one character vastly outpaces the others in combat. As one of the few mechanical situations where all players have to participate and one which has a lot of system, it can kind of stink when some of your characters have really cool styles of play that can't get enacted because the Dawn either wrecks everyone or gets into rocket tag with NPCs that the other PCs just can't handle.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's unfair of the Dawn to be good at combat and for a player to want to play a dope mega warrior. I'm not sure what the way is around the problem honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T14:56:21-07:00","id":924115,"title":"","content":"Some of my players, I know well enough that the caste they pick tells me a bit more than usual. <br /> <br /> When Player A tells me, &quot;I'm making a Dawn Caste!&quot;, he's <i>really</i> telling me, &quot;I made a character with a bunch of fives and fifteen combat Charms.&quot;<br /> <br /> When Player B tells me, &quot;I'm making a Night Caste,&quot; she's <i>really</i> telling me, &quot;I didn't have a concept in mind, so I'm throwing this one together ad-hoc.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say that they can't make good characters, it's just that with A and B, these particular, specific choices always seem a little predictable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T15:02:07-07:00","id":924121,"title":"","content":"As an aside to the Dawn issue with Supernals and combat balance: To me what it is saying when someone takes 5 in their Melee and 15 Melee charms and Supernal is &quot;I want all combats to be functionally trivial 90% of the time&quot;. So I run it that way. I feel like if you wanted combat to be challenging, why would you max out as hard as possible? Of course a Supernal Melee Dawn with 5 Melee, spec, and 5 Dex and 15 charms is gonna win 90% of the time. Thankfully, I can kinda gloss over that because it's obvious so combat gets shorter, not longer!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T15:04:51-07:00","id":924122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924121#post924121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside to the Dawn issue with Supernals and combat balance: To me what it is saying when someone takes 5 in their Melee and 15 Melee charms and Supernal is &quot;I want all combats to be functionally trivial 90% of the time&quot;. So I run it that way. I feel like if you wanted combat to be challenging, why would you max out as hard as possible? Of course a Supernal Melee Dawn with 5 Melee, spec, and 5 Dex and 15 charms is gonna win 90% of the time. Thankfully, I can kinda gloss over that because it's obvious so combat gets shorter, not longer!</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. And I think the player definitely isn't wrong to want to trivialize most enemies, or have the capability to solo Ahlat, or to fulfil whatever other metric they've decided is &quot;strong enough&quot; for themselves, because the ugly truth behind all the hard choices is that Exalted is pretty much a power fantasy, and I'm not going to deny that to somebody who just wants to KNOW that they could turn the room into fine red mist in two combat rounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","name":"nihnoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11456_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T16:03:35-07:00","id":924157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924121#post924121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an aside to the Dawn issue with Supernals and combat balance: To me what it is saying when someone takes 5 in their Melee and 15 Melee charms and Supernal is &quot;I want all combats to be functionally trivial 90% of the time&quot;. So I run it that way. I feel like if you wanted combat to be challenging, why would you max out as hard as possible? Of course a Supernal Melee Dawn with 5 Melee, spec, and 5 Dex and 15 charms is gonna win 90% of the time. Thankfully, I can kinda gloss over that because it's obvious so combat gets shorter, not longer!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where player intent and game design come into conflict.<br /> <br /> I believe many people feel that if they want to focus on a given Ability roll, then they need to get as many points in it as a they can. So if someone wants to be investigator because they like murder mysteries and such, then they need to get 5 dots in Investigation, 5 dots in Perception and grab a bunch of Investigation Charms. But, in reality, when you do that, it doesn't make murder mysteries more interesting - instead it <i>trivializes</i> murder mysteries.<br /> <br /> When the player is faced with a mystery, instead of actually spending multiple scenes and time investigating, putting clues together and coming up with a theory and then confronting the suspect after an intense and prolonged investigation (which is probably what the player who just got done reading a bunch of Agatha Christie stories wants) they just spend some Essence, activate some Charms, point at the target and, boom, the mystery is solved.<br /> <br /> The same thing is true for any other field - if a player wants to focus heavily on his character being a performer so he makes out Performance and Charisma and backs it up with Performance Charms, then his character is <i>already</i> the greatest performer in Creation and almost any &quot;challenge&quot; that the ST comes up with is going to be trivial.<br /> <br /> In other words, there's an inherent tension in the system - the more heavily you specialize in a given field, the less time you will need to spend dealing with that field in the game, since any challenges are more likely to be trivial. It seems rather counter-intuitive but it's better to think that specializing in a field is not something you want to do because you enjoy that field and want to spend a lot of time dealing with that field, but rather the opposite - that you want to <i>skip</i> that field and deal with it less in the game than you otherwise would.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to deal with Investigations in game, then make a super Investigator so you can just steamroll those mysteries. If you don't like combat, then make a super combat character so you can steamroll those enemies and get the combat scene over quicker<br /> <br /> This is something I think a lot of people don't understand. So a player wants combat to be a focus because they like making fighty characters and they enjoy the combat system. So they design a badass warrior, max out their stats for combat, grab a bunch of combat Charms... and then grumble when combat is over in two rounds because the enemies died so quickly. This in turn pressures the ST to create challenges for that super-specialized player (because he's understandably not having any fun), but at the same time the players who aren't specialized don't feel like they are really contributing.<br /> <br /> The ST comes up with a super-duper mystery to challenge the player with maxed Investigation stats and all of the Investigation Charms and then the other players, none of whom are invested in Investigation, are kind of stuck on the side because there isn't any chance that a character who <i>isn't</i> super-duper invested into Investigation would have a chance to solve the mystery in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> tl;dr I think you are absolutely right Paranoia, it's just that most players and ST's don't really understand this because it's so counter-intuitive - it just seems obvious you would invest in something you like doing and want to spend a lot of time doing, rather than invest in something you <i>don't</i> like doing and don't want to deal with. But essentially, that's exactly what ends up happening a lot of the time in Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-30-2016, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T16:55:46-07:00","id":924174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924098#post924098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While not actually a problem in either of the two games i'm involved in I see potential problems with trying to balance a supernal-combat dawn with a less-fighty party.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had problems like that in 1E and 2E. A combat focused Dawn with combat competent circle mates. All his favored abilities supported combat. Ahoy, Fighty McFighterton! He'd wipe the floor with the opposition. So, I had to create special antagonists just for him. Antagonists who were artificially augmented with incredibly high soak, or occasional minibosses like Noumu from My Hero Academia. Or flood him with tons of extras that kept him busy. Meanwhile, the rest of the party would deal with the encounter/mooks/boss fight I actually had in mind. The players never seemed to catch on and all had fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T17:43:22-07:00","id":924192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924077#post924077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. That sucks. Serenity is my favorite Sidereal Caste. Venus' chosen are so much more than prostitutes <b>(not that some of them aren't courtesans</b>). My first Serenity was a Traveling Musician who mourned his dead Solar Son and my second was basically a Righteous Devil cowgirl who carried a set of Flame pieces called &quot;Peacemakers&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking my experience to heart, that some is 'all of them except two'. I feel like the 2e book is kinda to blame, where it describes the main house of Venus and her chosen as a pleasure palace of untold beauty and stuff. So every serenity seems to be a young beautiful sex kitten, even if they do have some actual talents (like, your cowgirl could easily still fit these, from what was said so far of her - though I will assume she did not). My own Serenity was a seven foot tall craftswoman using Quicksilver Hands of Dream style to manipulate the dreams of others, and give people happiness in life via creating the stuff of their dreams in reality, and that was fun. But if you ask what caste I dread having other people play? That's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T18:08:32-07:00","id":924203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924192#post924192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Taking my experience to heart, that some is 'all of them except two'. I feel like the 2e book is kinda to blame, where it describes the main house of Venus and her chosen as a pleasure palace of untold beauty and stuff. So every serenity seems to be a young beautiful sex kitten, even if they do have some actual talents (like, your cowgirl could easily still fit these, from what was said so far of her - though I will assume she did not). My own Serenity was a seven foot tall craftswoman using Quicksilver Hands of Dream style to manipulate the dreams of others, and give people happiness in life via creating the stuff of their dreams in reality, and that was fun. But if you ask what caste I dread having other people play? That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. The description of the Division of Serenity does lead itself to a pleasure house. Though, when I think of &quot;Chosen of Serenity courtesan&quot;, I think Inara from Firefly, not sex fantasy kitten. I imagine most Sidereals (not just Joybringers) get offered some basic courtesan training, and not all Joybringers have the personalities suited to the courtesan lifestyle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T18:15:16-07:00","id":924206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924157#post924157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tl;dr I think you are absolutely right Paranoia, it's just that most players and ST's don't really understand this because it's so counter-intuitive - it just seems obvious you would invest in something you like doing and want to spend a lot of time doing, not invest in something you <i>don't</i> like doing and don't want to deal with. But essentially, that's exactly what ends up happening a lot of the time in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. This is a great observation and explains why some of Exalted characters fall flat and others are pretty awesome. Your supernal ability should not be the key that solves the plot, but the vehicle that gets your character to plot. This is something I'll have to think about more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:11:29-07:00","id":924221,"title":"","content":"The whole combat imbalance thing is one of the reasons that, on the rare occasions I get to play instead of ST, if I decide to make a warrior they are likely to be Resistance supernal - largely unkillable, but not leagues above other characters in terms of delivering ass-kickings","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T19:45:27-07:00","id":924243,"title":"","content":"I haven't had enough 3e experience to have any issues in the present, but back in 1e I used to get really steamed about players picking the Twilight Caste solely for the anima power, for characters who didn't otherwise do anything Twilighty.<br /> <br /> I remember one guy who showed up with a Twilight who had <i>only</i> Melee Charms -- including, thanks to flaws, Steel Devil Style (back when that was an Essence 4 Melee Charm). I guess he did have three dots each in Lore and Occult, clever scholarly fellow that he was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T20:44:27-07:00","id":924270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924243#post924243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't had enough 3e experience to have any issues in the present, but back in 1e I used to get really steamed about players picking the Twilight Caste solely for the anima power, for characters who didn't otherwise do anything Twilighty.<br /> <br /> I remember one guy who showed up with a Twilight who had <i>only</i> Melee Charms -- including, thanks to flaws, Steel Devil Style (back when that was an Essence 4 Melee Charm). I guess he did have three dots each in Lore and Occult, clever scholarly fellow that he was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, you too had problems with Murderlights at your tables. They're the bloody worst.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T21:04:30-07:00","id":924278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924157#post924157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">tl;dr I think you are absolutely right Paranoia, it's just that most players and ST's don't really understand this because it's so counter-intuitive - it just seems obvious you would invest in something you like doing and want to spend a lot of time doing, rather than invest in something you <i>don't</i> like doing and don't want to deal with. But essentially, that's exactly what ends up happening a lot of the time in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points all. I think this is why i enjoy characters with a wider focus. Instead of picking one thing to be OGM stompy bestest ever in, pick two to be great in, and a third to be good in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11915-wandering-swordman","name":"Wandering Swordman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11915_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T21:27:22-07:00","id":924288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924033#post924033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify further, multiple of these Twilight players are, as players, a fount of lore, facts, and general hyper-specific knowledge about Exalted from an OOC perspective, and it's just ASSUMED as a Twilight, they know this stuff, and it is their &quot;role&quot; to act in this hyper-specific and confident manner about this minutae. Almost like the Twilight is the skin they wear to justify their particular brand of annoying gaming, like how Tot above described a Caste managing to play badly to the proclivities of the player. Twilight is the signpost for me that maybe this person might &quot;love the game too much&quot; and have no social sense about scene stealing or making other people's experiences worse with their authority, or wants to use the game to dramatically edit the canon setting with their projects and (importantly), that is the primary or only reason they play.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924041#post924041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twilight: Hide in the Manse until you're Essence Five, then churn out infinite Artifacts and built servitors to make everyone else obsolete. Ignore anything that isn't 'know everything about the First Age' and 'Remake the First Age'- tied with Zenith for the whole 'Recreate the First Age'. Most likely to demand trips to Malfeas to make pacts with Demons for artifacts or w/e; I expect plenty of Transhumanism and Industrial Revolution literature and stuff from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I quote these two posts because they point to a very similar issue; namely, &quot;what's so goddamn great about the First Age that you feel that anything not done recreating it is wasted time?&quot;<br /> <br /> Twilights themselves seem to be the ultimate nerd power fantasy. Cast powerful spells with your almighty throbbing wizardbrain! Make cool toys so your friends will appreciate you! Be cleverer than anyone else alive!<br /> <br /> But at the same time, I'm not averse to playing a Twilight. I do want to give crafting a shot. The whole Twilight setup is a little...unsettling, is all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924070#post924070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-Solar wise: Chosen of Serenity. I fucking hate them. I have ran 4 sidereal games, and played in 7, as well as had a handful of experiences with only a Chosen of Serenity in a mix-splat game. In all but two games (one where I was the Chosen of Serenity!) the Chosen of Serenity has been every bad, childish sex obsessed loose as can be prostitute character that they are stigmatized as. Almost all of them would take 'sexy' ways of fighting, and wear no clothes but oh we have discrete essence armor so we can be basically naked. The worst one I ever played with was an absolutely terrible player who didn't even try to hide that every bit of his (I assume it was a guy, despite playing a girl) character was just a sex joke. Giant E cup breasts, an artifact armor they literally called the 'Victorious Secret' or something like that... ugh.I hate Serenities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't the signature Chosen of Serenity a butch mace-wielding happy-go-lucky woman-loving-woman? I wonder where they get this nonsense from.<br /> <br /> I think &quot;Victorious Secret&quot; is hilarious, but I'm not disputing your experience. I'm sure that these people were an endless stream of innuendo and that it got old quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11538,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","user":"kingcrackers","date":". 07-01-2016, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T21:57:15-07:00","id":924296,"title":"","content":"I've been blessed to play with mostly tolerable people playing mostly tolerable characters, and the extent to which any of those characters has been irritating is independent of caste.<br /> <br /> So I don't really have a lot to contribute to this thread other than to confirm that &quot;Victorious Secret&quot; is absolutely hilarious and I'm stealing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T22:09:22-07:00","id":924299,"title":"","content":"See, I'd make skimpy artifact armor and call it Victorious Secret... But I'd only USE it for a game where everybody agreed out of hand that this wasn't going to be a very serious game.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Shiny Chucklefucks and Their Misadventures&quot; is where I'd use Victorious Secret. A game wherein we have to consolidate political and mystical power because there's a Third Circle who's going to try and kill us all come next Calibration is <i>not</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T22:21:21-07:00","id":924301,"title":"","content":"Victorious Secret, for those curious, was a special artifact 5 star metal articulated plate, that's special abilities was that A. it wasn't actually articulated plate (it was lingerie, giant bra for said e cup, and a thong), B. applied penalties to any enemy who could see it, meaning said player walked around in their underwear or a robe that could easily be removed 99% of the game, and C. also made any seduction attempts superntural influence, so long as the target could see the awesome underwear. In exchange for all this it uh... made Arcane Fate even stronger, so no one could ever rememeber you, like ever? Except for the player, that was more like another bonus.<br /> <br /> The other people in the game were all super serious fate ninjas, in a quest to stop Fate itself from unwinding itself. T, the player whose full name I wont use, was just utterly terrible at doing anything, and their first response to any NPC existing was 'i try to seduce it'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","user":"KittyEmpress","date":". 07-01-2016, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T22:29:45-07:00","id":924303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924301#post924301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Victorious Secret, for those curious, was a special artifact 5 star metal articulated plate, that's special abilities was that A. it wasn't actually articulated plate (it was lingerie, giant bra for said e cup, and a thong), B. applied penalties to any enemy who could see it, meaning said player walked around in their underwear or a robe that could easily be removed 99% of the game, and C. also made any seduction attempts superntural influence, so long as the target could see the awesome underwear.<br /> <br /> The other people in the game were all super serious fate ninjas, in a quest to stop Fate itself from unwinding itself. T, the player whose full name I wont use, was just utterly terrible at doing anything, and their first response to any NPC existing was 'i try to seduce it'</div> </div> </div> </div>To be completely fair, this is precisely why Life Without Compunction was invented.<br /> <br /> &quot;It worked, didn't it? I don't see why you're making such a big deal out of this.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;She stopped the widow's haunting by seducing the husband's ghost and riding him like an angry Lunar!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Exactly. That woman's a hero!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;In FRONT of the widow! And their CHILDREN! In the middle of the orphanage they set on fire!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Would you have the audacity to do the same?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You're out of your minds, all of you.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Eh, you had to be there.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T00:05:14-07:00","id":924327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924115#post924115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of my players, I know well enough that the caste they pick tells me a bit more than usual.<br /> <br /> When Player A tells me, &quot;I'm making a Dawn Caste!&quot;, he's <i>really</i> telling me, &quot;I made a character with a bunch of fives and fifteen combat Charms.&quot;<br /> <br /> When Player B tells me, &quot;I'm making a Night Caste,&quot; she's <i>really</i> telling me, &quot;I didn't have a concept in mind, so I'm throwing this one together ad-hoc.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say that they can't make good characters, it's just that with A and B, these particular, specific choices always seem a little predictable.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a somewhat tangential note, one of the things I find very refreshing about the new edition is that the complete ditching of Nature and Motivation for the more nuanced 'at least four distinct intimacies' system of defining a character has forced me to take 'stock' characters who only had the broadest element of backstory in First and Second edition, and develop backstories that actually worked. Hence how my Dawn Caste 'Ex-Immaculate Monk' spontaneously grew a backstory involving getting booted from the House of Bells and having his arranged marriage ruined by a prissy Dynast who was bullying the janitorial staff into stealing the opposing side's strategy notes for the next wargame, and my Night 'World's Greatest Thief' grew a backstory involving stealing the last imperial tribute Thorns ever assembled just as the zombies were coming up to the gate, only to give it all away to people crowded at the docks and stealing the ship which his criminal syndicate had intended to use to ditch out of the city with the loot, only now loaded down with refugees instead of money. The new ruleset has pushed me to do more with these stock characters in getting them on the sheet... and I'm getting deeply annoyed at that, because if there's likely to be an Exalted game around here, I'm almost inevitably going to be the one running it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T02:31:15-07:00","id":924366,"title":"","content":"I am not a 100% sure about third edition, but in first and second editions, at least, the Eclipse Caste was potentially problematic due to their diplomatic immunity.<br /> <br /> I played one in a mini-series in which the main antagonists were Fair Folk and a subplot involved a demon. I invoked that immunity several times and I see how, with a less conscious player and a less experienced storyteller, it could have been a problem.<br /> <br /> Here, only one encounter was not eventually fought. The rest of the encounters were simply preluded by a couple of minutes of dialogue before the punching. But potentially the Caste Ability of the Eclipse Caste could have robbed the warrior types of their chance to shine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T04:37:54-07:00","id":924393,"title":"","content":"Third Edition has changed the Dawn Caste in a way I find really interesting by making them the people most qualified to learn the softer Martial Arts.<br /> It initially seems rather jarring for a Martial Art like Silver-Voiced Nightingale which because of previous experiences feels like an outgrowth of someone's skill as a musician rather than something that the most combat orientated caste would pick as a specialty but when you think about the sort of musician who'd actively think &quot;yes, I want to make sonic attacks and kill people with my zither&quot; the Dawn Caste association makes a lot more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T04:51:33-07:00","id":924397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924301#post924301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Victorious Secret, for those curious, was a special artifact 5 star metal articulated plate, that's special abilities was that A. it wasn't actually articulated plate (it was lingerie, giant bra for said e cup, and a thong), B. applied penalties to any enemy who could see it, meaning said player walked around in their underwear or a robe that could easily be removed 99% of the game, and C. also made any seduction attempts superntural influence, so long as the target could see the awesome underwear. In exchange for all this it uh... made Arcane Fate even stronger, so no one could ever rememeber you, like ever? Except for the player, that was more like another bonus.<br /> <br /> The other people in the game were all super serious fate ninjas, in a quest to stop Fate itself from unwinding itself. T, the player whose full name I wont use, was just utterly terrible at doing anything, and their first response to any NPC existing was 'i try to seduce it'</div> </div> </div> </div>This is like. A quadruple pun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T05:16:48-07:00","id":924399,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Deleted because I screwed up a quote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":11875,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","user":"Rowanas","date":". 07-01-2016, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T05:20:19-07:00","id":924400,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I've already stated a dislike for Eclipse caste (at least I can remember their name now). While some people have pointed out interesting ideas for a bureacracy themed Eclipse, the very idea just doesn't engage with me. I very much doubt I'll ever play one unless I'm doing it for a joke, and even then, there are better jokes.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924393#post924393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;yes, I want to make sonic attacks and kill people with my zither&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> My backup character is a lunatic Night Caste, who kills people by stopping their heart-song. Mechanically it's SVN, but it fits into his Night caste-ness. Given that it runs almost entirely off of performance, it seems like the &quot;soft&quot; MA that -least- fits the Dawn. I get your point, and I don't disagree, but you picked the worst example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T06:21:27-07:00","id":924418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kingcrackers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924288#post924288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder where they get this nonsense from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's because most of Bluesid related things all have sex and addiction as a theme for some reasons, from their SMA to Venus herself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T07:27:29-07:00","id":924438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924418#post924418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's because most of Bluesid related things all have sex and addiction as a theme for some reasons, from their SMA to Venus herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yuuuup. 2E really leaned hard on the sex-positive/sex-as-power theme, and in some cases the text was just plain bungled.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","user":"Totentanz","date":".  Removed the rest to post in the new thread. 07-01-2016, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T09:33:30-07:00","id":924499,"title":"","content":"My first-ever Exalted character was a Chosen of Serenity. On one hand, diving headfirst into the Sidereal end of the pool was probably not the greatest idea and drove me to more stress than necessary.<br /> On the other hand, I think I made a pretty decent Joybringer, at least in terms of not making her a Chosen of Tiddy---she was a matchmaker, storyteller, and the group's fabulous mom.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the thread's main topic---neither in 2E or 3E so far have I found a particular caste to be a problem, at least in my fairly limited experience. Problems have universally seemed to be about the player rather than the caste. Of course, I've only played and never ST'd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T11:19:29-07:00","id":924547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924041#post924041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that there are 'bad sterotypes', but nothing that would throw up a red flag to me. It's more like 'if someone is going to play one of these, if they're one of THOSE players, they're probably going to play up on these stereotypes'; so these are just 'if I see someone saying that they have a bad player in this caste, I'm gonna assume it's this issue'<br /> <br /> Dawn: Gotta kill Everything. No Peace, No Negotation. 100% Fatality Rate, kill, maim and murder anything that even slightly stands against you, never give a second chance. Generally gonna be the most 'Murder-hobo', will probably have just 'found' an Artifact somewhere and not really care about it. Most likely to have already killed a Wyld Hunt in their backstory before the game started.<br /> <br /> Zenith: If the Dawn browbeats everyone outside of the group, the Zenith browbeats everyone in it. They play up the fact that only they get messages from the Sun and that this means they expect everyone to fall in line and listen to them immediately; their goals are the most important and they will never change their mind. Most likely to demand the recreation of the First Age. In 2E, expect them to favor Melee and other Combat Stuff and expect the Dawn to allow them to be their equal in combat. Equally likely as the Dawn to forgo redemption in favor of blowing the shit out of everyone.<br /> <br /> Night: Spend as much time as possible hiding from everyone, including the party. The longer the party doesn't even know you exist, the better. Sneak around, try to spend as little time with the party as possible. Lie to the party and otherwise misinform them, be clear that you trust no one and nothing in the party. Often has some other 'boss' they're reporting to. Despite this, will often not actually DO anything; expect them to hide but only hide around the party, instead of going to retrieve information.<br /> <br /> Twilight: Hide in the Manse until you're Essence Five, then churn out infinite Artifacts and built servitors to make everyone else obsolete. Ignore anything that isn't 'know everything about the First Age' and 'Remake the First Age'- tied with Zenith for the whole 'Recreate the First Age'. Most likely to demand trips to Malfeas to make pacts with Demons for artifacts or w/e; I expect plenty of Transhumanism and Industrial Revolution literature and stuff from them.<br /> <br /> Eclipse: Social Fu everyone and everything, the same as the Zenith. Get into fights with the Zenith over who the actual leader of the Circle is, invest in Beaucracy and expect infinite everything to fall into your lap. Use Oaths on Everything you can find, go to Heaven and find Gods to learn whatever charms you can find from Gods, preferably the most overpowered ones. Secretly as munkiny as the Twilight but using the God Charms instead of Crafting stuff</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm tempted to repost this on 1d4chan and/or /tg/.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T10:06:16-07:00","id":924923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924041#post924041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eclipse:...Use Oaths on Everything you can find... </div> </div> </div> </div>This is the most annoying thing ever, as a player or ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11915-wandering-swordman","name":"Wandering Swordman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11915_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T00:15:31-07:00","id":925245,"title":"","content":"There are definitely problematic concepts, though luckily these days my player group, being more mature and experienced, rarely play them. And there are concepts that don't fit well together. This, I'd say, is the main issue I see; as I've run this Exalted game for about 5 years (with a long hiatus in the middle), 3 of the PCs are old, 3 are new, and it can be difficult for new PCs to fit in with the old, if they have different worldviews or methods (not helped by the fact the old PCs have different worldviews, and strong ones, but are friends due to their long time together).<br /> <br /> But castes? No, I don't find any problematic. If I had to choose, I'd choose Dawn, because while several of the PCs are good at combat (they are Essence 5 afterall, it's difficult not to be), they're not amazing at it, for their experience level, and that's fine because they're generally fighting Dragonblood or less experienced people. Their current enemies are a circle of Essence 3 Solars. So a really combat-orientated Dawn might be problematic as he'd just smash through combats and enemies I made to challenge him would be deadly for anyone else. But a)for essence 5 Solars, even social or mental ones, not much is deadly, especially in 3e, in 24 sessions they've yet to even get crippled, and b)I learnt the trick a long time ago, of having one deadly opponent as the boss who engages the best combatant, and lieutenants who fight the others.<br /> <br /> Also, a Dawn did recently join the group. He has 20 war charms, and more bureaucracy charms (about 5) than he does offensive charms (Excellent strike). He has artefact super-heavy plate and about 10 resistance charms, so he'll be basically unkillable, and I guess his initiative will rise without me being able to stop it, but he shouldn't be mullering any opponents too quickly. So it's fine.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T06:44:14-07:00","id":925318,"title":"","content":"I have no preferences or dislikes among castes as far as being a Storyteller is concerned. Castes are a nice set of distinctions that encourage roleplaying while not being terribly intrusive. My players play them all with about the same sort of frequency with Eclipse and Night perhaps the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1546,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","user":"Great Cthulhu","date":". 07-03-2016, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T06:53:29-07:00","id":925319,"title":"","content":"Whatever Caste I'm playing.<br /> <br /> There can be only one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T07:46:08-07:00","id":925334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rowanas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=924400#post924400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I get your point, and I don't disagree, but you picked the worst example.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T08:11:47-07:00","id":925349,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=925334#post925334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=925319#post925319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever Caste I'm playing.<br /> <br /> There can be only one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I now really want to make a Solar with Highlander themed charm reskins and a nice big two-handed claymore with evocations revolving around lightning and sucking out the soul, like a sword made of Yasal crystal that stores the sweet, sweet vim of my slain opponents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This post was made in a factory where hyperbole and sarcasm are handled.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11875-rowanas","name":"Rowanas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11875_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T14:11:42-07:00","id":932631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/923927-solar-ish-which-castes-do-you-want-to-see-least-at-your-table?p=923999#post923999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much an observer here but yeah, I have a related question about the Perfect Circle ideal: Whether in practice it tends to be easier to ST and play a Perfect Circle set up that's the idealised set up for Exalted - same splat methodology, about 5 different areas of role focus within that. Or a set up where you have like, a Slayer, a Dawn, a Dusk, a Full Moon meet up... where you have characters with the same general goal and focus - they're *all* about about the path of the warrior - with slightly different Exalt type variations. If anyone wants to bite on their experiences?</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience? Perfect Circle. Having everyone greatly skilled/focused in the same area/character concept like your combat example limited my story developing options. Although, there was one time where I ran a D&amp;D 3.5 rogues game. The rogues have so many ability points they were able to come up with a fairly diverse allotment of skills with some overlap that was beneficial. So, your example could be fun and I've done it before, but with a diverse group the story options were more numerous for me.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T14:50:19-07:00","id":932641,"title":"","content":"I'd prefer mixed abilities to having everyone be good at similar things, but... I think that trying to make sure everyone has different characters can lead players to make characters that aren't as interesting as the ones they'd have made if they weren't worried about it. Often people think &quot;oh, there's one of every caste except Zenith, so I'd better play a Zenith&quot; or &quot;there's already a Twilight, so I shouldn't play one&quot; and then they make a character they're less enthused by. Or make the character they were going to make anyway, but a different caste, and it doesn't work so well.<br /> <br /> So, what I'm saying is a Perfect Circle is kind of good, but it's not the most important thing, and its best not to worry about it too much. As long as you don't have 5 Dawns, or 5 Twilights, or something, it's best not to worry about it too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}